# Build context for containers/operator/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit prefers <dockerfile>.dockerignore over the repo-root .dockerignore.
# A dedicated file is required here: the root .dockerignore excludes profiles/,
# which this image must copy in.
#
# Allowlist style — exclude everything, then re-include only what the image
# needs. Keeps the context to a few hundred KB instead of the whole repo.
*
!km-config.yaml
!profiles
!containers/operator
!docs/km-config.example.yaml
# The terragrunt tree — ~1.3MB of .hcl/.tf, and what makes `km init --plan`
# possible in the image. The exclusions below matter more here than anywhere
# else in this file: an operator building from their own working clone has
# applied against it, so infra/ locally carries provider caches and, if they
# ran a local apply, state.
!infra
# Lambda zips only — NOT the rest of build/, which also holds cross-compiled
# sidecar binaries and a cached terraform. See KM_LAMBDAS in the Dockerfile;
# absent, the build falls back to the release asset.
!build/*.zip

# Never ship these even from the re-included paths.
**/.DS_Store
**/.terraform
**/.terragrunt-cache
**/terraform.tfstate*
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
# Tracked and empty upstream, but the build context is the operator's working
# tree, not a clean checkout. Nothing in the image reads it.
infra/live/.secrets.json
